+# Secure conversion: Simple Readable Metadata SG 2.5.4
+
+## Identity and scope
+
+Upstream https://github.com/ShammiG/ComfyUI-Simple_Readable_Metadata-SG,
+exact historical commit e51819a7944c526dc8a545c7ec82b73e450b57c9, release
+xe51819a. The registry 2.5.4 archive SHA256 is
+253fc479b7ecb6acc64d75a5d9d532646a7c3c77ec7b542e8857ed2b081e8e2c.
+All 19 pristine paths/bytes and Git blob identities/executable modes were verified
+against that exact historical tree and codeload payload; no live HEAD substitution.
+Corpus 0644 versus codeload 0664 group-write normalization is recorded separately.
+The complete MIT license (copyright 2025 ShammiG), README, workflows, original
+sources and inactive old-version RAR remain present. The RAR is never executed.
+
+The following are **bounded Mac development behavior recommendations** for
+coordinator review, not catalogue/count/deployment promotion. Python 3.13 runs
+the inherited unsealed development runtime without a dependency profile digest.
+Exact runtime, native dependency, source/resource and declaration identities are
+in source-provenance.json and the frozen handoff. No installation or weights.
+
+| Backend ID | Disposition | Scoped behavior evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| SimpleReadableMetadataMAXSG | supported | Exact 17-output native image/metadata math, ordered sampling-name schemas and drift refusal; required guest and production outer |
+| SimpleReadableMetadataSG | supported | Exact eight-output native pixels/mask/text/scalars across admitted formats and metadata; required guest and outer |
+| Simple Readable Metadata Text Viewer-SG | supported | Bounded original STRING/UI passthrough, zero capabilities, actual guest and outer |
+| SimpleReadableMetadataSaveTextSG | supported | Source token math, first-free naming, exact UTF-8 txt/json/md and native invalid-JSON fallback; managed output and actual guest |
+| SimpleReadableMetadataVideoSG | supported | Exact ten-output native OpenCV frame/FPS/stride/resize and tag precedence for measured codecs/profile; actual guest and outer |
+| SavePositivePromptSG | supported | Original STRING/UI and downstream saved PNG own-input/title/annotation intent via typed owner service |
+| SaveNegativePromptSG | supported | Negative analogue, actual saved PNG, permission denial, own/foreign prompt isolation |
+
+| Frontend entry | Disposition | Scoped behavior evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Simple_Readable_Metadata_SG.js | supported | Source properties/metadata readout choices and workflow reconstruction |
+| Simple_Readable_Metadata_MAX_SG.js | supported | Managed image selection, actual owned natural dimensions, preview/removal and state |
+| Simple_Readable_Metadata_VIDEO_SG.js | supported | Managed video selection, actual media dimension events and cleanup |
+| Simple_Readable_Metadata_Save_Text_SG.js | supported | Exact prefix placeholder, source minimum/initial sizing and output-file notification |
+| Simple_Readable_Metadata_Text_Viewer_SG.js | supported | Actual opaque worker/renderer selection, clipboard, filters, navigation, safe pretty data, serialization and teardown |
+
+## Census and contracts
+
+Exactly seven IDs and five extension registrations, no backend routes or
+frontend-only graph nodes. Three safe frontend helpers are served under the exact
+WEB_DIRECTORY web; recursive import/census is checked. The five original web
+filenames remain the entries. Archival Python modules remain unimported; active
+Python imports only loader_nodes/text_nodes and their bounded helpers.
+IDs, displays, categories, input ordering/defaults/options, force-input/tooltips,
+output names/types/cardinality and video numeric display="number" are preserved.
+Legacy function names migrate to V3 execute; this is not an algorithm change.
+
+The original image/video selectors list every immediate regular input file, not
+only media extensions. The published /secure-nodes/assets/input?kind=file retains
+that intent with sorted portable bounded logical names; no extension filter,
+recursion or fabricated empty option. Its explicit exclusions are outside/broken
+symlinks, special files and nonportable control/backslash/colon/invalid-UTF8 names.
+Selected nonmedia inputs retain native decoder failure and subsequent recovery.
+Upload and preview use managed inputs/view URLs; no arbitrary paths or fetch.
+
+MAX output combo lists preserve exact current canonical SAMPLERS/SCHEDULERS order
+in sampling_names.json/.py. Existing public models.sampling_names must match at
+execution; a changed list is visibly refused, not silently substituted or
+called a security rejection. MAX alone consequently requires models capability.
+
+## Backend computation and managed transport
+
+All extraction/formatting/model-name parsing remains in pack code. Image and
+video helpers mechanically retain the pinned source AST except bounded IO
+transport/schema/cache adapters. Tests compare unmodified selected source class
+methods; those test-only AST controls are not sandbox/import/whole-pack evidence.
+Fresh required Seatbelt guests and production outer dispatch separately exercise
+all seven actual exported classes and exact scalar/tensor types.
+
+Image input is <=8MiB encoded and <=4,194,304 pixels. PIL header/metadata and
+JSON lexical depth/items are admitted before retained pixel construction.
+Projected RGB/mask/float intermediate reserve is pixels*80+encoded bytes.
+Text/metadata <=64KiB UTF-8, <=4096 aggregate items and <=32 nesting levels;
+EXIF prompt JSON is included. Bounds are the supported workload, not source
+maxima, hard parser-heap or process physical-memory enforcement claims.
+
+Input transport uses assets.size, read_range(offset0,maximum), a separate
+one-byte tail at maximum, and re-size. Growth/shrink/length drift is refused
+before decode; read_bytes is never used. Real changing-file guest probes and
+sentinels verify bounded imports and denial/recovery. Same-size concurrent
+rewrites are not atomic snapshots; no immutable-file/host locking claim.
+Image fingerprint preserves source content SHA256. Video content digest plus
+source options deliberately replaces inaccessible host mtime identity.
+
+The source's positive_candidates NameError in some metadata paths occurs in
+both source and converted algorithms and retains native fallback; it is an
+upstream source defect, not a conversion security rejection.
+
+Video pixels use unchanged native OpenCV via exactly one guest-owned standard
+tempfile holding admitted encoded bytes; unconditional close/unlink applies on
+success, decoder errors and refusals. No host paths are exported, no subprocess,
+ffprobe, new scratch API or sandbox changes. Source frame/FPS/force/stride/resize,
+BGR conversion, masks, tensors and all ten outputs remain native-exact for
+MPEG4 and FFV1 controls. PyAV pixels demonstrably differed on MPEG4; that RED is
+preserved, never substituted or tolerance-relaxed. Only tags use bounded BytesIO
+Pillow/PyAV with measured native ffprobe/Pillow precedence/results.
+
+Video local profile: <=512KiB encoded, <=64 attempted decoded frames (EOF attempts
+included), <=2048 input dimensions, <=1,048,576 cumulative decoded pixels,
+<=8MiB outputs and <=16MiB conservative selected working reserve. These are
+preflight bounds before retained resize/color/output allocation. Native decoder
+parser peak memory and unsupported codecs are not certified by those bounds.
+Source max_frames0 remains "all" within that profile, not unbounded allocation.
+
+## Saved output and state lifetime
+
+SavePositive/NegativePrompt declare the original hidden context schema on the
+trusted plane but never receive/export hidden dictionaries as guest arguments.
+output.record_text_input derives the declared STRING from trusted execution
+inputs and binds the active node, then copies only its own input/title and
+host-ID-suffixed extra annotation. Actual downstream guest PNG saving verifies
+exact source annotation/pixels, foreign inputs unchanged, and output denial.
+No whole graph recovery, host hidden mutation through raw, user IDs or durable KV.
+
+SaveText preserves token/date math on the admitted guest clock, UTF-8 encoding,
+JSON pretty indent2/ensure_ascii=False and native invalid-JSON passthrough. Paths
+become confined logical output prefixes. The first-free scan is bounded4096;
+new_only publication refuses a competing writer instead of native race overwrite.
+Capability/security/broker errors are explicit, not broad-caught into the source's
+empty-UI write-error success. Native broad write-error controls remain recorded.
+Time zone/locale/clock identity is runtime-qualified, not authenticated host time.
+Managed output retention/import/download and Cloud user durability are separate
+host deployment concerns; there is no invented source-adjacent authored library.
+
+Viewer text, theme/wrap, filters, font and pretty display are workflow-serialized
+node state. Fresh reconstruction and node-instance isolation are tested.
+No process-global preference, browser storage or KV replaces workflow state.
+Pending clipboard work cannot commit after removal or an intervening revision.
+Frontend manifest grants only clipboard.read and clipboard.write; the actual
+worker harness derives those grants from that manifest, not fixture constants.
+Backend raw is limited to image/video owned numerical buffers, models only MAX
+sampling-name queries, output only declared writers/annotations, and assets
+only managed input reads/output counter queries. Viewer has no backend grants.
+
+## Frontend safety and deliberate adaptations
+
+All active behavior uses the published worker facade, mounted owned elements,
+typed widgets, managed previews/files and clipboard. No ambient document/parent
+DOM, same-origin authority, unrestricted network, prototype patching or eval.
+Real host/guest/renderer/broker controls complement hermetic regular matcher tests.
+
+TextViewer accepts bounded JSON and reviewed inert object-data syntax instead of
+the original eval fallback. Expressions/getters/functions cannot execute. All
+display and highlighted fragments are escaped. The metered regular-syntax
+profile has pattern256 UTF-16, input64KiB UTF-8, states512, transitions262144,
+results4096, data4096/depth32 and pretty-output262KiB limits. Backreferences,
+lookaround and unsupported syntax show a visible profile error, never literals.
+Native greediness/nonzero matching/line order and Unicode/surrogate boundaries
+are compared for the admitted profile. Zero-width iteration advances one UTF-16
+unit to repair the original default non-Unicode gi hang; original unsafe/hang
+diagnostics remain frozen. Unsupported regex/data is not silently evaluated.
+
+Readonly textarea value retains native CR/CRLF-to-LF normalization. A single
+extra initial LF in escaped serialized markup compensates the measured HTML
+parser stripping only when needed; actual displayed value and UTF-16 selection
+remain exact. Empty/one/multiple leading LF, CRLF, copy/paste and teardown are
+tested. Safe span highlights replace sanitizer-disallowed mark tags. Owned
+viewport240px with padding/border0 gives explicit navigation geometry, not legacy
+parent DOM access. Typed change/media events replace legacy polling.
+
+Browser preview is browser-codec dependent: the real media event fixture uses
+VP8 WebM. This does not certify MPEG4 browser preview merely because native
+OpenCV MPEG4 frame extraction succeeds. The test fixture is losslessly base64
+packaged for text-only patch reconstruction; decoded bytes match the original.
+
+## Evidence and remaining deployment qualifications
+
+Final commands/results, before/after selected runtime identities, all payload
+hashes/modes, manifest, pair and portable archive are in the immutable handoff.
+Focused suites run twice on unchanged final owned bytes, with bytecode/cache
+disabled and explicit COMFY_CORE_ROOT. Plain pair and deterministic ZIP both
+rebuild every V2 byte/mode from fresh complete pristine copies; tampering refuses.
+Historical fixture errors, missing models cap, PyAV mismatch, unbounded-read,
+leading-LF and schema REDs remain separate evidence; none are relabelled green.
+
+Dependencies are the measured Python3.13/Torch/NumPy/Pillow/OpenCV/PyAV versions,
+not a complete managed/sealed image. Native duplicate AVFoundation ObjC class
+warnings and Pillow I-mode/pynvml deprecations remain visible. There is no trained
+model computation, accelerator/GPU, Linux, authenticated Cloud, multi-server,
+parser hard-heap, codec universe, native storage-alias or deployment proof.
+Those requirements stay explicit rather than blanket-rejecting useful bounded
+local image/video/text behavior. Independent serial integration/count is root-owned.
